<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adolf Frederick II of Mecklenburg-Strelitz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1658">1658</a>–<a href="/years/1708">1708</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adolf <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a> of Mecklenburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strelitz">Strelitz</a> was the first duke of Mecklenburg-Strelitz. After a long succession dispute in the Mecklenburg house, the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a> of 1701 gave him the eastern Stargard lands and the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratzeburg">Ratzeburg</a> as a separate duchy. When his residence burned in 1712 his successors built the new town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neustrelitz">Neustrelitz</a>, and his line ruled until 1918.</p></div>
